Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

* ci(upstream-sync): run all eight Python slices; two slices hit tests.yml's 30 min timeout

* fix(desktop): a reloaded window resumes a streaming segment from a snapshot, not a replay it may miss

session.resume on a canonical session now carries the streaming segment's text so far
(inflight, segment_only), cut under the stream lock with last_sequence. A fresh socket
has no replay cursor, so the tail streamed while history painted before the subscription
was lost (reattach-running-turn.spec.ts: reply never reappeared / lost its tail).
Renderer: apply the snapshot to the warm streaming row; flush the inflight journal on pagehide.
E2E: hold the resume request so the whole held tail lands in the gap (deterministic repro).

* fix(desktop): a segment snapshot cut before the turn settled never repeats the committed reply

* test(web): avoid repeated library checks in freshness fixture [daveey]

* fix(kanban): a frozen legacy alias no longer restores links on an open card [daveey]

Removing a shepherd subscription on the owner did nothing: the pre-qualification
copy of the card stays in the replica forever and the fold copied its links back
(109 of them on one card), so a chat stayed tied to a card it had only read. An
open twin publishes every live link itself; only a finished twin still takes the
alias's links, for the terminal release.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* test(gateway): the resume snapshot fake carries the inflight field the real snapshot now has

* fix(kanban): an external gateway drain holds dispatcher claims like a deferred restart [daveey]

The embedded dispatcher gated only on _restart_requested, so an external
drain (.drain_request.json) kept claiming into a gateway that refuses
every new worker: MacBook 10-30 09:12-09:26 and 09:39-10:06 spawned 0 for
up to 48 ticks and the stuck warning blamed profile health.

_external_drain_active now sets gate=drain (suppress_spawn ticks,
bad_ticks 0), the hold logs one INFO line at start naming the drain
principal and since-time (read via gateway.drain_control) and one at
release, and stuck_warning only fires on ungated ticks.

* fix(kanban): a worker may archive a done card its own task created [daveey]

A scratch waiter a worker creates for a live proof is claimed when it wakes and
completed by its own worker. The creator rule only allowed unclaimed cards
(the misplaced-copy cleanup from 4f6e223fe84, which refused done cards with no
stated reason), so the creator could never archive it and six such waiters
leaked on 10-30. A done card with no live claim and no open card listing it
as a parent may now be archived by its creator, as done capability owner cards
already could. Running/claimed cards, done cards with open children, foreign
cards and the worker's own task are still refused.

The archive-scope rules move to hermes_cli/kanban_archive_scope.py (re-exported
from hermes_cli.kanban) to keep kanban.py under its line cap.

* fix(kanban): archiving a placement-forwarded card archives its remote copy [daveey]

* fix(sessions): a lost request outranks live work, a cron is not a wait, a refused turn is replayed [daveey]

A chat ended on 'Your request was not processed', painted as waiting because it
owned a cron, so the person's two requests sat unseen for 18 h. Reading the
outcome: any open card or cron beat the failed turn, and a recurring cron can
never end, so that wait was permanent.

- _lost_request: a typed or steered message that failed or got no answer is
  unresolved even with open cards (a held declaration and a real reply close it).
- Crons leave the wait list; a finished chat is done and names them in crons;
  the Desktop keeps the loop glyph, in the green of done.
- A retryable refusal keeps its turn marker and replays through auto-continue
  after 45 s and 180 s with the existing guards, boot sweep included.

