* fix(desktop): a resume snapshot merges with the deltas that beat its answer, by stamped offset [daveey]

The canonical session.resume cuts the streaming segment's snapshot when it
subscribes the new socket, so deltas published after that cut can reach the
renderer before the resume answer. Reconcile then rebuilt the live row from
the snapshot alone (or kept it only when the live text happened to start
with the snapshot), dropping those deltas until message.complete repaired it.

Backend: SessionEvents tracks the snapshot's span in the stamped stream
(turn_id, segment, UTF-16 offset/end) and sends it as inflight.segment_stamp.
Re-sent overlapping deltas are counted once, a stale segment is ignored, a
gap or boundary (interim seal, tool call, null delta) restarts the span, and
unstamped text claims no span.

Renderer: a live text part records the stamped offsets its trailing text
covers (streamSpan), and appendAssistantTextPart admits stamped text by
offset. The snapshot merges with the row's stamped run by offset (warm row),
and a cold resume grafts the runtime state's early deltas onto the snapshot
row. The journal overlay carries the projection's span. No text comparison
decides an overlap when a stamp is present.

* fix(desktop): a warm activation keeps the resume snapshot under a delta that beat its answer [daveey]

The warm session.activate path reconciled the stamped segment snapshot onto
the cache read before the RPC, then overlaid rows that changed during it by
identity. A stamped delta past the snapshot's cut that reached the cached
live row while the RPC was in flight made that row the overlay winner, and it
never held the snapshot's range: the reply painted 'A2 NEXT ' instead of
'A2 TAIL NEXT ' until message.complete.

After the overlay (or the occurrence-aware reconcile), merge the snapshot
under the adopted pending row by offset when its closing stamped run is in the
snapshot's segment and does not already cover the snapshot's span.

Test: warm-activate-early-delta.test.tsx failed (RED) for both the canonical
(history rows) and omitted-history activate answers when the delta painted
before the answer; current-segment.test.ts covers the helper's MEDIA source
and no-op guards.

* fix(desktop): a warm activation streams into the snapshot row, and a tail snapshot keeps the row's earlier text [daveey]

Two cases the stamped resume snapshot still lost:

- A warm cache with no live row (the turn started while this window was
  away) got the snapshot's assistant-stream row from the projection but no
  stream target: the cleared-clarify spread wrote state.streamId (null) back,
  so the next delta opened a second bubble ('A2 TAIL ' | 'NEXT'). The warm
  reconcile now targets that pending row while the turn runs.
- A snapshot whose span starts past zero (the backend restarted its span past
  a gap in its own stream) replaced the row's closing text, dropping stamped
  text the row held before it ('NEXT ' instead of 'A2 TAIL NEXT '). When the
  row's run starts before the snapshot's, the snapshot now lands on it by
  offset.

Tests: warm-activate-early-delta.test.tsx (no-live-row case, both history
shapes) and current-segment.test.ts (nonzero-start snapshot) were RED first.

* refactor(desktop): move the warm path's snapshot-row and early-clarify overlay phases into their siblings [daveey]

pendingSnapshotRowId (resume-reconcile.ts) and overlayCacheWithoutEarlyClarify
(early-clarify-projection.ts) carry the warm activation's existing logic out of
resumeSession; withoutEarlyClarifyProjection takes an absent request id as a
no-op. Behaviour unchanged. Adds a reload case with no journaled row: the
cold path's graft alone keeps the early delta (red without it).

